{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:08af2b6c9f67153c","name":"G1-M4-C Dunelizard Fighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-08af2b6c9f67153c","title":"G1-M4-C Dunelizard Fighter","revision":20648,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:14:50Z","sha256":"e7f365bd2efeb5931c91bc60ffb3197ba7ff615ac1dfd1fa2df5ebfc906e64a0","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20648","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=G1-M4-C%20Dunelizard%20Fighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-08af2b6c9f67153c","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Dunelizard is a medium fighter designed primarily for use by small planetary defense forces, mercenaries, and powerful corporations. First produced by MandalMotors during the period between ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," and the Galactic Civil War, the Dunelizard was originally offered to, and rejected by, the Imperial Navy. An Imperial advisor placed to oversee the operations of the company did not want MandalMotors to suffer major financial losses under his direction and thus approved limited sales of Dunelizards to other forces. Because the Empire had already passed on the design as too expensive and underpowered, the official position of the advisor was that Dunelizards in the hands of non-Imperial pilots posed an insignificant risk to Imperial forces.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In truth, the Dunelizard is a basic but adaptable Starfighter that has served as the primary ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," of more than one flight wing. It is especially popular with pirate groups and smugglers due to its rugged nature and the ease of making repairs (any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Repair"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Repair"}," a Dunelizard Fighter gains a +1 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus). The fighter can be modified easily, and though the basic model has Linked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"},", it is easy to swap out these weapons for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Cannons"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missile Launchers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missile_Launchers"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Proton Torpedo Launchers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Proton_Torpedo_Launchers"},"; each launcher has a six-mission payload.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Dunelizard also has a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," and a simple ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputer","referenceId":"reference:4ae152610571a224"},", but it lacks a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Socket"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Socket","referenceId":"reference:b6e7b59b72abbbc5"}," that would allow the calculation of more advanced hyperspace coordinates. A popular modification of the Dunelizard involves removing the Copilot's seat and installing a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Socket"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Socket","referenceId":"reference:b6e7b59b72abbbc5"}," in the cockpit behind the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"},". However, the design of the ship's wings reduces the visibility of an Astromech Droid at that port location, a problem that led to the Type II Dunelizard- a version with a shorter, narrower wing configuration.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["G1-M4-C Dunelizard Fighter Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 27; +8 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 140; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 10; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"},": 25; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 47\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Fly 15 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Character_Scale"},"), Fly 4 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.mir